{
  "_doc": "Panel-key RESOLUTION corpus (STATUS-jas item 8 class L, step 2). A case resolves a normalized key chord {key, ctrl, shift, alt, meta} (a missing modifier is false; a single letter is matched upper-cased) against the `keyboard:` rows of one panel in the compiled bundle, found at ANY depth (layers.yaml's are on its tree_view, artboards.yaml's on the panel). Rows are tried in order; a row matches when its key string parses to the same chord AND its `enabled_when`, if any, is true in `ctx`. The action may be a {{...}} template, evaluated in `ctx`. String params are expressions evaluated in `ctx` (a bare identifier that reads null is its own name, as a `dispatch` effect's are). `expected` is {action, params}, or null when no row matches. Modifiers use the shortcuts.yaml vocabulary: Ctrl is the platform command key (the Mac binding maps Command to it), so a Meta row is never written. A case may give `panel_spec` (an inline panel) instead of `panel`: no shipped panel binds one chord twice, so the ORDER law (first enabled row wins; a disabled row falls through) is witnessed only by synthetic rows.",
